---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Gameplay of DeathEmpire';
const description = 'Forge your legacy: allegiance, preparation, risk and consequence shape who you become in DeathEmpire.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} lang="en" enPath="/DeathEmpire/gameplay/" esPath="/DeathEmpire/es/gameplay/">
  <article>
    <header>
      <p class="section-eyebrow">GAMEPLAY</p>
      <h1>Forge your legacy</h1>
      <p>Your place in DeathEmpire will not be decided by a single path. It will be shaped by allegiance, preparation, risk and consequence — whether you serve order, hunt relics, study Mana or lose yourself to corruption.</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>The Pillars</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-header"><h3>⚔ Combat &amp; Specialization</h3></div>
          <div class="card-body"><p>Build a path that suits your choices and style: warrior, rogue, mage, cleric or specialist — each with a clear bond between archetype, role, weapon and playstyle.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-header"><h3>🔮 Exploration &amp; Risk</h3></div>
          <div class="card-body"><p>Discover places that may change what you become: Wild Mana zones, star craters and ruins where every advantage has a cost, a history and a risk.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-header"><h3>👁 Factions &amp; Reputation</h3></div>
          <div class="card-body"><p>Loyalty opens doors and closes others. Serve the Inquisition, hunt with the Star Hunters, or walk alone among the Free Survivors.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-header"><h3>💀 Equipment &amp; Progression</h3></div>
          <div class="card-body"><p>Craft, refine and carry gear that tells your story — from Star Shard steel to relics of the old Empire.</p></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Development Note</h2>
      <p>Gameplay systems are in active development. What you read here describes the direction of the project, not a promise of immediate availability. Systems still taking shape are marked <span class="status-badge status-dev">In development</span>.</p>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <p><a href="/DeathEmpire/">Back to home</a> · <a href="/DeathEmpire/roadmap/">Follow the Roadmap</a></p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
